worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_program_ir.js"
  ceiling 369
  rationale "Issue #1138 pure browser coding IR, bounded typed fragment search, source attribution, and honest unverified lowering parity with native composition. Since the meanings seed split (issue #960 R222-1) the browser fragment catalog bootstraps meanings-coding-structure-2.lino as a second seed part, mirroring src/coding/fragment_catalog.rs bootstrap_from (+4). IrType::OrderedSequence unification parity with the native rules (ordered unifies into sequence, never the reverse) added +14. Wiring the closed-program selection module into the complete-candidate filter, carrying application counts for least-action selection, and the binder-mention slot preference added +13. The ceiling moved 338 to 369 to record that parity work; candidate-selection logic itself lives in formal_ai_worker_closed_programs.js."
